# Reviewed warnings that `make synth` accepts. Every other warning fails it.
#
# `@vcpu/rtl-tools synth-summary` collects each line of the Yosys and nextpnr logs that starts with
# "Warning:" (or "ABC: Warning:", ABC's own output inside a Yosys log) and matches it against the
# regular expressions below, one per line, in JavaScript syntax. The comment block above each
# expression is its review and is copied into the summary. docs/hardware/synthesis-guide.md#warnings
# explains each one at more length. Add an entry only after reading the warning and deciding the
# design is correct as it stands; never to silence a real problem.

# ABC is handed only the combinational part of each module, because Yosys keeps the flip-flops
# itself. ABC notes that this network has no latches and so needs no sequential optimisation.
# It says nothing about the design.
^ABC: Warning: The network is combinational

# nextpnr-ice40's timing estimate misses the 12 MHz target on the iCE40UP5K: the longest path runs
# through the single-cycle combinational divider. The ticket reports this as measured instead of
# changing the RTL; the summary records the achieved Fmax and meetsConstraint: false. The
# iterative divider (DIV_IMPL=ITER, research/cpu/experiments/div-impl/) meets the target, so its
# run does not print this. Only this exact message form is allowed.
^Warning: Max frequency for clock '[^']+': [0-9.]+ MHz \(FAIL at [0-9.]+ MHz\)$

# Only with the iterative divider (DIV_IMPL=ITER), in the iCE40 flow: ABC9 notes that the output of
# one carry box (an SB_CARRY; the variant's new carry chain is the divider's trial subtraction,
# whose borrow selects both the quotient bit and the next remainder) feeds more than one node
# inside the network it optimises, so it maps around that box rather than through it. It is a limit on ABC's optimisation, not a
# fault in the design: the same run's `&verify` reports "Networks are equivalent", and the divider
# is checked exhaustively by test-divider and by make verify DIV_IMPL=ITER. Only this message form,
# with no complex flops, is allowed.
^ABC: Warning: AIG with boxes has internal fanout in 0 complex flops and [0-9]+ carries\.$
